    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nI have already submitted an issue on coc(https://github.com/neoclide/coc.nvim/issues/5758), and the author of coc mentioned that this is a problem with neovim itself.When using the new version of Neovim (specifically Nvim development/prerelease builds or Nvim 0.12.5), some floating windows pop up and obstruct my input, as shown in the screenshot below.However, this issue does not exist in older versions of Neovim(Nvim 0.11.7).My terminal is either the VS Code terminal or Tabby.\n\n<img width=\"1352\" height=\"1157\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4082165f-6873-4c16-b7e4-f14b7c7c7a19\" />\n\n<img width=\"1831\" height=\"625\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/83363827-a548-409a-bdf4-f1722849ab21\" />\n\n<img width=\"1786\" height=\"1378\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2bd86483-c9ef-47a5-8e6c-26d1dfc628ab\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nThis bug occurs randomly and can be reproduced after writing more code.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe floating window does not block the input.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNvim 0.12.5\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWindows\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nvscode 1.137.0\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nother(download from github)",
